    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d517">

                <pb facs="0737" n="635" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg635"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">765.84/899: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Atherton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-08-21T19:00:00+01:00">August 21, 1935—7
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 21—1:15 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>388. Cabinet members have been in consultation today with the leaders of the
                    Opposition, the Dominion representatives and representatives of the Committee on
                    Imperial Defence. In the given circumstances importance is attached here to Mr.
                        MacDonald’s<anchor n="62" xml:id="d517-f1"/> statement to the press just
                    before the Cabinet met this afternoon: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“I regard the present situation as the most serious thing we have had to
                            face since 1914. It is a very grave situation.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Atherton</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d517-f1" n="62" xml:id="d517-f1-content">
                <p>J. Ramsay MacDonald, British Prime Minister.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
